            <ArticleTitle>Double-wire technique for access into a protruding aorto-ostial stent for treatment of in-stent restenosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>214-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of restenosis following ostial stenting of the right coronary artery with protrusion of the stent into the aorta. Treatment was only possible after a guidewire advanced through a lower strut was used to lever the guide, and a second guidewire was advanced through the true lumen.</AbstractText>
